# Regenerable environments and build trees
.venv/
engine/build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# The exported fixtures ARE tracked (56 MB): they are what makes every
# bit-exactness claim in the README checkable by anyone who clones this, and
# the raw corpus they came from is too large to ship.
#
# Large regenerable artifacts. Everything here is reproducible from
# original_code/ via spark_pipeline/export_fixture.py and engine/bench/run_bench.py;
# the evidence that matters (bench JSON/CSV, figures, env capture) stays tracked.
original_code/python/data/

# Overlap-band fixtures are DERIVED from a tracked fixture by a tracked tool
# (tools/make_overlap_fixtures.py, ~26 s), so they are regenerable from what
# this repository already ships and would otherwise duplicate item_full's CSR
# arrays twice over (~22 MB). The pair-count subsets are not ignored: those
# need the 457 MB raw corpus, which is not shipped.
data/fixtures/*_ovl_flat/
data/fixtures/*_ovl_skew/

results/*.model
results/*.sims.bin
results/*_predict.json
results/bench/*.bin

# Nsight traces are NEVER tracked. nsys records the profiled process's
# environment into the trace, and the RunPod hosts used here had
# RUNPOD_API_KEY and JUPYTER_PASSWORD set -- both .sqlite and .nsys-rep
# carried live credentials. GitHub push protection caught it; the traces were
# purged from history. Everything derived from them (tools/nsys_overlap.py
# output) is already written up in docs/analysis.md, which is the part worth
# keeping. If you re-capture, `unset RUNPOD_API_KEY JUPYTER_PASSWORD` first
# and check with `strings <trace> | grep -E 'rpa_|PASSWORD='` before adding.
results/profiles/

# This repository is public. Personal working documents and scratch output
# directories are kept outside the tree and must never be committed here.
# A backstop, not the mechanism: nothing matching these rules has ever been
# tracked, and the point is to keep it that way if a stray file lands in the
# working tree.
outputs/
work/
*.docx
*.doc

original_code/python/result/
original_code/scala/result/
original_code/scala/target/
data/sources/
original_code/scala/project/target/
original_code/scala/out/
data/fixtures/*_lane_full/
data/fixtures/*_lane_tail/
